---
// src/components/SupportedImageFormats.astro
---
<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto my-14 px-4">
  <div class="text-center mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">Supported Image Formats</h2>
    <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm md:text-base mt-2">Explore the strengths and primary use cases for every supported export format.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
    <!-- 1. WEBP -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">WEBP</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">WebP Image Format</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Developed by Google, WebP provides superior lossless and lossy compression for web images. It keeps files significantly smaller than PNG or JPG while retaining rich color depth, helping websites load faster and improving Core Web Vitals.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 2. AVIF -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">AVIF</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">AV1 Image File Format</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">An ultra-modern format powered by the AV1 video codec. AVIF delivers exceptional compression efficiency even at tiny file sizes, preserving high-fidelity textures, HDR brightness, and transparency better than almost any legacy image standard today.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3. JPG -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">JPG</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Joint Photographic Experts Group</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">The universal standard for digital photos and everyday web viewing. JPG utilizes lossy compression to balance reasonable file sizes with natural photographic detail, making it compatible with virtually every operating system, browser, and camera device worldwide.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 4. PNG -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">PNG</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Portable Network Graphics</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">The go-to lossless format designed specifically for clear graphics and transparent backgrounds. PNG prevents blur around crisp edges and fine text, making it ideal for brand logos, UI icons, screenshots, and artwork that require true alpha transparency.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 5. GIF -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">GIF</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Graphics Interchange Format</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">A classic 8-bit bitmap format limited to 256 colors that famously supports frame-by-frame animation loops. While larger than modern video formats, GIF remains universally supported across messaging apps, social platforms, and simple animated web banners.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 6. BMP -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">BMP</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Bitmap Image File</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">An uncompressed raster format created by Microsoft to store raw pixel data without quality loss. Because it lacks advanced compression, BMP files are large, but they ensure exact pixel-by-pixel rendering across desktop software and older systems.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 7. ICO -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">ICO</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Icon File Format</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">A specialized container format used predominantly for website favicons and Windows application desktop shortcuts. An ICO file can bundle multiple resolutions and color depths into a single asset, ensuring clean display across diverse screen scales.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 8. PDF -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">PDF</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Portable Document Format</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Developed by Adobe to present documents and visual layouts reliably regardless of device or software. Converting images into PDF creates universal, print-ready files that are easy to view, email, and archive without unexpected formatting shifts across platforms.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 9. SVG -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">SVG</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Scalable Vector Graphics</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">An XML-based vector format that scales infinitely to any screen dimension without pixelation or quality loss. Perfect for website logos, interface illustrations, and vector icons, SVG files remain crisp, lightweight, and directly editable in design tools.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 10. HEIC -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">HEIC</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">High Efficiency Image Container</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Apple's standard photo container for iPhone and iPad camera captures. HEIC stores photos at roughly half the file size of traditional JPEGs with superior 16-bit color depth, though converting to JPG or PNG is often necessary for universal Windows sharing.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 11. TIFF -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">TIFF</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Tagged Image File Format</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">A flexible raster format favored by professional photographers, graphic artists, and desktop publishers. TIFF supports lossless storage to retain uncompressed master quality during repeated editing cycles, making it the industry benchmark for commercial print and archival scanning.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 12. TGA -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">TGA</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Truevision Targa Graphic</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">A legacy raster format widely utilized in 3D modeling pipelines, video game engines, and texture rendering. TGA natively stores raw alpha channels and uncompressed pixel buffers, allowing real-time game engines to read bitmap layers efficiently without decoding overhead.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 13. DOCX -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">DOCX</div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Microsoft Word Document</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">The standard OpenXML word processing container used across Microsoft Office and Google Docs. Converting images into DOCX wraps your visual assets neatly into an editable document layout, ready for business reports, university assignments, and immediate text additions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
